{"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Actions-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/AI-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/App-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Autocomplete-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Callouts-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Clipboard-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Dictation-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Emojis-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/External-Keyboards-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Feedback-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Fonts-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Host-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Layout-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Localization-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Navigation-Article"],"generated":true}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Autocomplete-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Dictation-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Host-Article"],"title":"Related Articles","anchor":"Related-Articles"}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/keyboardkit\/plugins-article"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"This article describes the KeyboardKit plugin engine.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Plugins-Article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"KeyboardKit ships with plugins that can be used to extend the core SDK with additional functionality. Plugins are stand-alone and don’t know that KeyboardKit exists, and vice versa."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plugins are used to provide 3rd party integrations, isolate system API usages, and contain code that requires certain permissions. This lets developers choose whether to use a plugin or not, by considering the implications it would have on the app."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"How to use a plugin","anchor":"How-to-use-a-plugin","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can add plugins to an app or keyboard extension when you add KeyboardKit to the project, or at a later time. Once you have linked a plugin, you must import it where you’ll use it. Most plugins just require a single import, since they are injected at a single place."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Plugins use basic values to simplify mapping between a plugin and the main library. For instance, the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/DictationEngine","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" uses tuples to stream text and volume data. Plugin types often require a single line of code to conform to a KeyboardKit protocol."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Available Plugins","anchor":"Available-Plugins","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Below is a list of available plugins that ship with KeyboardKit. You can use the same plugin architecture to implement your own plugins."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Autocomplete","anchor":"Autocomplete","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"KeyboardKitAutocompletePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" has advanced "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/AutocompleteEngine","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"s that can improve autocomplete for certain locales.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To use this plugin, you must link it to your keyboard extension and import it where you set up KeyboardKit. You can then inject its engine when calling ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardInputViewController\/setupKeyboardKit(for:completion:)","type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import KeyboardKit","import KeyboardKitAutocompletePlugin","","extension PluginAutocompleteEngine: @retroactive AutocompleteEngine {}","","class KeyboardViewController: KeyboardInputViewController {","","    override func viewWillSetupKeyboardKit() {","        super.viewWillSetupKeyboardKit()","        setupKeyboardKit(","            for: .myApp,","            autocompleteEngine: pluginAutocompleteEngine(...)","        )","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Engines that require downloaded resources can either download these automatically or require the app or user to call "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/AutocompleteEngine\/download(_:onProgress:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". To add download support to the main app, you can inject the engine into the "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppView","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import KeyboardKit","import KeyboardKitAutocompletePlugin                 ","","extension PluginAutocompleteEngine: @retroactive AutocompleteEngine {}","","@main","struct MyApp: App {","","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            KeyboardAppView(","                for: .myApp,","                autocompleteEngine: pluginAutocompleteEngine(...)","            ) {","                ContentView()","            }","        }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This will automatically enable downloads from within the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardLocaleSettingsScreen","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". You can also use the same engine to implement standalone download support elsewhere in the app.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This plugin currently has a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".langlot(...)"},{"text":" engine that integrates with a 3rd party engine. This engine requires a separate license to be used, which you must pass in when you create the engine. More engines will be added in future versions.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can use an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/AutocompleteEngineCollection","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" to combine multiple autocomplete engines into one. This will be usable when we add more engines in the future.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","style":"important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When using autocomplete engines that require manual downloads, make sure to use an App Group-based language store to allow the main app target and its keyboard extension to share downloads.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Important"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Dictation","text":"Dictation","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"KeyboardKitDictationPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/DictationEngine","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that you can use to set up dictation in your app. This engine wraps all the code that requires Info.plist permissions, which means that you must only add these permissions if you use this plugin."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To use this plugin, you must link it to your main app target and import it where you set up the app. You can then inject its engine into the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppView"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import KeyboardKit","import KeyboardKitDictationPlugin","","extension PluginDictationEngine: @retroactive DictationEngine {}","","@main","struct MyApp: App {","","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            KeyboardAppView(","                for: .myApp,","                dictationEngine: pluginDictationEngine","            ) {","                ContentView()","            }","        }","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppView"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps the engine instance alive, to use a single instance even if the app body is re-evaluated again. You can also inject an engine with the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/keyboardDictation(withEngine:)"},{"type":"text","text":" view modifier if you’re not using the app view."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"important","name":"Important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Dictation"},{"type":"text","text":" developer guide for important considerations when setting up dictation for an app and its keyboard extension."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"},{"text":"Host Application","anchor":"Host-Application","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyboardKitHostPlugin"},{"text":" has a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"